% Goal

Implement and maintain `brain/api/api_plan_arrange.py` as the THE SINGLE READ THE ARRANGE TAB NEEDS, deliberately one call: ordered tracks, effective notes with their layer (plan|global) and diverged flag, derived-then-merged segments, active bunches with their member spans, per-file revs, the composite rev and staleness. Because it is one response, refresh cannot render a mix of old and new state. Each segment carries its author so attribution renders without a second fetch. Each active bunch carries bunch_id AND its member span so the UI can draw an un-bunch control without another round trip. A plan with no built mix returns the order with segments: [] rather than 404, so a brand-new plan is arrangeable immediately. The response is also the PREVIEW surface for the built candidate order before Start mix, including any reorder performed by NemoClaw, H Company, or Feel-only planning. Emits the composite rev as an ETag. READ-ONLY: journals nothing.

% Product contract

- Preserve the exact public interface declared in `<pdd-interface>`.
- Treat the reviewed architecture description in this prompt as normative behavior.
- Keep plan identity, immutable track identity, revision guards, and non-destructive storage semantics intact across GUI, CLI, and agent callers.
- Preserve compatible behavior outside this module's stated responsibility; do not redesign unrelated mixing or playback logic.
- Reject malformed, stale, ambiguous, or unsafe writes explicitly instead of silently losing plan data.
- Keep the implementation deterministic where the contract describes deterministic behavior.
- Target Python 3.13+ for Python modules and baseline browser JavaScript without a bundler for browser modules.
- Inspect the current implementation, its declared dependency modules, and the focused tests before changing code. This is a brownfield source prompt: working, tested behavior not contradicted here remains part of the contract.

% Architecture detail

THE SINGLE READ THE ARRANGE TAB NEEDS, deliberately one call: ordered tracks, effective notes with their layer (plan|global) and diverged flag, derived-then-merged segments, active bunches with their member spans, per-file revs, the composite rev and staleness. Because it is one response, refresh cannot render a mix of old and new state. Each segment carries its author so attribution renders without a second fetch. Each active bunch carries bunch_id AND its member span so the UI can draw an un-bunch control without another round trip. A plan with no built mix returns the order with segments: [] rather than 404, so a brand-new plan is arrangeable immediately. The response is also the PREVIEW surface for the built candidate order before Start mix, including any reorder performed by NemoClaw, H Company, or Feel-only planning. Emits the composite rev as an ETag. READ-ONLY: journals nothing.

